      "area": "Isolated Pillow workers",
      "change": "Resolve the adjacent decoder through itov.dataset_images for source and wheel execution under -I. Read L-mode fingerprint intensities as scalar bytes and check extrema. Preserve resize, orientation, fingerprint and padding semantics; RGB/L pre-change vectors match exactly."
    },
    {
      "area": "Plans and candidate lifecycle",
      "change": "Literal overloads distinguish workflow bytes from hash-only asset checks. Checked JSON objects support plans, bindings and specifications. Explicitly reject missing retirement, rollback and replay entries before unpacking or indexing."
    },
    {
      "area": "Review, checkpoint and media records",
      "change": "Checked object decoding and result contracts cover loader requests/results, review documents, tensor headers, image-check inputs, saved media records and FFprobe output. Optional evaluation, checkpoint parameters, graph nodes, artifacts and FFmpeg paths are validated before use."
    },
    {
      "area": "Workflow and platform typing",
      "change": "Give graph collections, rotation state, trigger-distance maps and Windows child records their actual types. Recognize Windows/POSIX lock branches through sys.platform. Keep malformed standalone workflow failures durable and prevent submission."
